35
00:07:35,260 --> 00:07:37,820
Thank you, Ryan, and welcome everyone.

36
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:42,460
I'm Andy Gutmanns, Vice President and General Manager of Google Data Cloud.

37
00:07:42,920 --> 00:07:51,120
Across every industry, organizations are moving past simple chatbots to autonomous AI agents, actively executing work in production.

38
00:07:51,120 --> 00:08:00,160
Today, we'll explore the key architectural shifts behind this transformation, and see how our agentic data cloud empowers you to lead the way.

39
00:08:00,814 --> 00:08:03,480
Now, not that long ago, we were entering the agentic era.

40
00:08:04,100 --> 00:08:09,900
Today, we're seeing customers like yourselves getting significant benefits from running agents in production.

41
00:08:11,086 --> 00:08:18,820
The opportunity to capture new revenue streams, drive efficiencies, and better manage risk is just too big to ignore.

42
00:08:18,820 --> 00:08:25,520
We're hearing from most of you that re-imagining how your enterprise operates with agents is top of mind.

43
00:08:25,870 --> 00:08:29,740
And we're already seeing leading companies doing this in production today.

44
00:08:30,286 --> 00:08:36,220
For example, Virgin Voyages deployed over a thousand agents to transform how they run their business.

45
00:08:37,102 --> 00:08:49,100
Their marketing agent, Email Ellie, writes personalized campaigns, dropping production timelines from six weeks to just days, driving a 28% increase in sales.

46
00:08:49,520 --> 00:09:01,580
Their operational agent, Ruby, automatically orchestrates mass itinerary rebookings during severe weather, cutting a six-hour manual process down to just 11 minutes.

47
00:09:02,254 --> 00:09:06,380
We consider three fundamental shifts that define this transformation.

48
00:09:06,380 --> 00:09:17,780
First, we're moving from human scale to agent scale, introducing orders of magnitude more workload as agents operate your business around the clock.

49
00:09:18,894 --> 00:09:25,580
Second, is the shift from practitioners being individual contributors to becoming orchestrators of agents.

50
00:09:26,574 --> 00:09:38,860
And third, is reactive intelligence to proactive action, moving past architectures that tell us what happened yesterday to agents executing in real-time on your behalf.

51
00:09:39,182 --> 00:09:47,500
The legacy architectures some of you are running right now, such as first-generation lake houses, break at agent scale because of three structural failures.

52
00:09:48,206 --> 00:09:56,780
The walled garden demands you move your estate into siloed environments, fracturing security, trapping your data, and blocking real-time action.

53
00:09:57,358 --> 00:10:09,900
The trust gap misleads many into thinking a good model and a technical data catalog log is enough for quality results when you really need rich context to ensure agents drive the right outcomes.

54
00:10:10,480 --> 00:10:18,480
And lastly, the cost spiral, which risks your costs exploding when you try to scale autonomous agents on a fragmented stack.

55
00:10:18,940 --> 00:10:25,860
Many vendors talk about their data platforms as a system of intelligence, but a system of intelligence is reactive.

56
00:10:26,798 --> 00:10:29,040
It waits for a human to ask a question.

57
00:10:29,040 --> 00:10:35,620
What you need is a system of action that is proactive and can operate on your behalf.

58
00:10:36,526 --> 00:10:38,520
It needs you to provide three things.

59
00:10:39,406 --> 00:10:48,100
First, the ability to safely activate all your data, including the 90% that is dark and trapped in unstructured formats.

60
00:10:49,166 --> 00:10:59,580
Second, the trust for true autonomy, grounding agents in governed enterprise contexts so they make reliable, compliant decisions on your behalf.

61
00:11:00,078 --> 00:11:18,200
And third, re-imagining the practitioner experience, elevating them from being individual contributors who work in a co-assistant model with AI to orchestrators of agents who are driving intent-driven outcomes through business understanding, human creativity, and judgment.

62
00:11:18,894 --> 00:11:25,260
And you need it all on an AI native vertically integrated data platform, avoiding the cost spiral.

63
00:11:25,940 --> 00:11:30,020
This is why we built the world's first agentic data cloud.

64
00:11:30,670 --> 00:11:44,220
This data cloud was designed for the agentic era, helping you solve for data silos without a walled garden approach, driving differentiated accuracy and trust, and doing this all at the lowest possible cost.

65
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:48,900
Now underpinning all of this is Google's AI hypercomputer.

66
00:11:49,358 --> 00:11:51,360
We didn't stitch together rented hardware.

67
00:11:51,360 --> 00:12:02,260
we own the full AI native stack delivering real impact like running AI functions in BigQuery and AlloDB up to a hundred times faster and cheaper.

68
00:12:02,830 --> 00:12:09,240
And to activate all that data and break down walled gardens brick by brick, we built the borderless lake house.

69
00:12:09,940 --> 00:12:22,040
The reality is your data lives everywhere, on Google, across other clouds, on premises, and even your SaaS applications like SAP, Salesforce, or a ServiceNow.

70
00:12:22,740 --> 00:12:34,160
Vertically integrated and built on an open Apache Iceberg, it connects your multi-cloud, SaaS, and operational data into one governed foundation without needing to move it.

71
00:12:34,740 --> 00:12:40,700
In fact, Apache Iceberg data under management has more than tripled over the past year.

72
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:52,980
Instead of moving data, stitching together connectors, or paying surprise egress fees, you get a stack tuned at every layer from the network to the engine.

73
00:12:54,100 --> 00:12:57,620
And today, we're announcing new enhancements for the borderless Lakehouse.

74
00:12:58,360 --> 00:13:01,020
Gemini now works directly on your Lakehouse.

75
00:13:01,660 --> 00:13:11,420
Business users can use natural language to query records that live across clouds, while AI agents can ground their reasoning and generate code from the same data.

76
00:13:13,820 --> 00:13:27,960
With cross-cloud interconnect and caching for AWS and Azure, which is now generally available, your agents can gain context across clouds with a private, secure connection and zero variable egress fees.

77
00:13:28,580 --> 00:13:37,920
And the Borderless Lakehouse integrates directly with Knowledge Catalog, which automatically indexes your distributed data, including unstructured data in cloud storage.

78
00:13:38,574 --> 00:13:48,240
This gives agents just enough context to be accurate while controlling token costs, helping you develop an intelligent and sustainable agentic strategy.

79
00:13:48,878 --> 00:13:52,580
We see this at Commerzbank, one of Germany's largest banks.

80
00:13:53,390 --> 00:13:57,780
They wanted to deploy AI agents across contact centers and marketing.

81
00:13:58,862 --> 00:14:06,480
But in a bank, you face strict regulatory compliance, and they refused to lock their data into a closed proprietary silo.

82
00:14:07,342 --> 00:14:12,100
They solved this by building on our borderless lake house using Apache Iceberg.

83
00:14:12,100 --> 00:14:23,200
Separating storage from compute, let them point AI models at their existing data without moving it while enforcing compliance rules in a single open storage layer.

84
00:14:24,302 --> 00:14:29,100
That foundation cut their marketing campaign production from weeks to just days.

85
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:39,580
And in their contact centers, it gives their agent-assist systems the live context to describe calls and serve verified next steps in seconds.

86
00:14:40,110 --> 00:14:47,360
Now, we're continuing to expand what the Borders Lakehouse means by using it to bridge your transactional and analytical systems.

87
00:14:48,020 --> 00:14:58,400
Today, we're announcing Direct Iceberg Access in AlloyDB, letting you query iceberg tables stored in cloud storage without any ETL pipelines or copies.

88
00:14:58,958 --> 00:15:05,780
You can now join live operational data with historical lakehouse data in a single Postgres query.

89
00:15:05,780 --> 00:15:17,640
And it is fully integrated with the Lakehouse Runtime Catalog allowing you to register iceberg tables in AlloyDB alongside the rest of your tables.

90
00:15:18,580 --> 00:15:25,600
Everything automatically shows up in the Knowledge Catalog, so your agents get the same government context across both.

91
00:15:26,360 --> 00:15:29,500
Now activating all of your data is only the start.

92
00:15:29,998 --> 00:15:37,600
You also need the processing engines that can handle autonomous agentic workloads at scale and ours continue to lead the industry.

93
00:15:38,720 --> 00:15:44,520
BigQuery is the market leading serverless analytic system and it keeps getting better.

94
00:15:45,240 --> 00:15:54,140
In the past year alone, we've made queries over 35 percent faster while cutting query processing costs by more than 40 percent.

95
00:15:55,310 --> 00:16:00,180
Our lightning engine now runs Spark almost five times faster than open source.

96
00:16:01,582 --> 00:16:13,020
Spanner is the multi-model database enterprise choice for demanding use cases like core banking applications or digital twins for autonomous network operations in telco.

97
00:16:14,414 --> 00:16:20,280
We run Google's billion user services on Spanner like YouTube, Ads, and Gmail.

98
00:16:21,838 --> 00:16:31,200
And lastly, AlloyDB is the Postgres database chosen by companies to modernize off legacy databases like SQL Server or Oracle.

99
00:16:31,982 --> 00:16:39,700
It runs many times faster than standard Postgres and has a special database architecture to power millions of live agents.

100
00:16:40,494 --> 00:16:45,440
These engines power the most demanding, mission-critical workloads for global enterprises.

101
00:16:46,222 --> 00:16:48,720
And today, we're making them even better.

102
00:16:49,380 --> 00:16:58,520
BigQuery Graph is now generally available, bringing petabyte-scale graph analytics directly on relational tables with zero ETL.

103
00:17:00,210 --> 00:17:11,010
It allows organizations to model data as nodes and edges to uncover complex, hidden relationships without needing to move the data into a separate graph database.

104
00:17:11,410 --> 00:17:15,130
And today, two new models from Google Research run natively in BigQuery.

105
00:17:15,726 --> 00:17:25,230
The first is Times FM 3.0, now in preview, which lets you generate forecasts directly in SQL with no custom models to train or manage.

106
00:17:25,230 --> 00:17:33,570
It's a state-of-the-art foundation model designed to unlock native, multivariate time series forecasting inside BigQuery.

107
00:17:34,190 --> 00:17:44,810
The second new model from Google Research is TabFM, also now in preview, a zero-shot foundation model that brings predictive machine learning directly into BigQuery.

108
00:17:45,550 --> 00:17:55,250
It eliminates the traditional time-consuming machine learning lifecycle of manual feature engineering, hyperparameter tuning, and custom model training.

109
00:17:55,930 --> 00:18:06,990
And on the Spark side, managed service for Apache Spark extends its price performance advantage over leading market alternatives by over three times through further improvements to Lightning Engine.

110
00:18:07,598 --> 00:18:11,570
We're releasing improvements such as faster startup at no additional cost.

111
00:18:12,270 --> 00:18:17,350
This is beneficial for both interactive workloads and small batch ETL jobs.

112
00:18:17,998 --> 00:18:25,710
In addition, performance-optimized mode allows data teams to align infrastructure tiering directly with workload urgency.

113
00:18:26,330 --> 00:18:31,330
It runs on Google's top-tier compute fleet, and Lightning Engine is turned on by default.

114
00:18:32,046 --> 00:18:34,430
Now let's turn to your operational databases.

115
00:18:35,330 --> 00:18:38,850
Earlier this year, we talked about the million-agent world.

116
00:18:39,662 --> 00:18:41,450
It's arriving faster than expected.

117
00:18:42,254 --> 00:18:47,970
We're moving from single co-pilot interactions to networks of agents collaborating simultaneously.

118
00:18:48,814 --> 00:18:58,530
When they reason and act all at once, sudden traffic spikes can overwhelm your core databases, competing with your business applications for resources.

119
00:18:59,230 --> 00:19:08,830
To power these million agent scenarios, we've driven continuous innovation to ensure our engines scale elastically at reasonable, predictable cost.

120
00:19:09,330 --> 00:19:11,650
That's why we built Fluid Scaling in BigQuery.

121
00:19:12,174 --> 00:19:29,230
It was designed specifically for the spiky nature of agent workloads, giving you instant, zero-touch elasticity with true per-second billing and no minimums, lowering costs by up to 34% on average for auto-scaling workloads.

122
00:19:29,630 --> 00:19:33,490
Also, recently, we announced Postgres for Agents in Adobe DB.

123
00:19:34,010 --> 00:19:50,850
It provisions reader nodes in seconds to handle bursty, ephemeral agentic traffic directly on live operational data and scales compute straight back to zero when demand subsides, delivering real-time decision-making with pay-as-you-go efficiency.

124
00:19:51,550 --> 00:19:54,370
And this builds on Data Boost in Spanner and Bigtable.

125
00:19:54,926 --> 00:20:11,810
By using independent serverless compute that queries our underlying storage layer directly, agents can execute massive read workloads with full workload isolation, completely bypassing your provisioned database nodes without impacting transactional SLAs.

126
00:20:12,430 --> 00:20:14,330
That isolation isn't theoretical.

127
00:20:14,810 --> 00:20:32,470
UKG, one of the leading enterprise workforce platforms, set out to build autonomous agents that could execute multi-step workflows across HR and scheduling, like catching pay discrepancies before payroll runs, reallocating shifts, and flagging compliance risks.

128
00:20:33,006 --> 00:20:37,450
UKG solved this by building their People Fabric platform on AlloDB.

129
00:20:38,390 --> 00:20:47,310
AlloDB provides millisecond-level read-after-write performance, giving agents live data while isolating their workloads from core transactions.

130
00:20:48,110 --> 00:20:51,110
Today, over 1,000 organizations are live on the platform.

131
00:20:51,530 --> 00:21:00,110
Their workforce agents reason over live signals and take action across payroll and scheduling with zero impact on production operations.

132
00:21:00,110 --> 00:21:09,330
And we're also announcing AlloDB Express in Preview, designed for builders and autonomous coding agents who need extreme development velocity.

133
00:21:10,062 --> 00:21:22,790
It offers sub-two-second provisioning, scale-to-zero pause, and secure private IP connectivity, and a small footprint with one to two vCPUs and 20 gigabytes of storage.

134
00:21:24,260 --> 00:21:30,980
AlloDB now provides developer-first Postgres environment for agent development and testing.

135
00:21:31,566 --> 00:21:40,500
We recently announced the general availability of Spanner Omni, bringing Google's legendary multi-model database engine beyond our own data centers.

136
00:21:41,166 --> 00:21:53,280
Now you can bring that Google-grade consistency, scale and power right to your own infrastructure, running anywhere across clouds, on-premises or even on your laptop.

137
00:21:54,260 --> 00:21:56,120
So that's the foundation and the engines.

138
00:21:56,800 --> 00:22:00,900
Now, once your data is active at scale, the next challenge is making sense of it.

139
00:22:01,600 --> 00:22:06,900
Our agentic data cloud provides a deep understanding of your business context through the Knowledge Catalog.

140
00:22:07,300 --> 00:22:16,548
Knowledge Catalog delivers context that drives the highest quality and trusted outcomes while in parallel reducing token costs and processing costs.

141
00:22:17,006 --> 00:22:34,120
It autonomously aggregates metadata and semantic context from all your sources, including operational databases, analytical data, third-party catalogs, and unstructured data like business documents, and even your SaaS applications like SAP or Workday.

142
00:22:34,958 --> 00:22:43,560
Through Gemini-powered enrichment, it automatically maps complex relationships and continuously learns how your enterprise actually uses its data.

143
00:22:44,110 --> 00:22:54,120
And when agents need to act, they query this knowledge with Google-powered search that enforces your security permissions so they only retrieve what they're authorized to see.

144
00:22:54,958 --> 00:23:05,000
And it even saves tokens by giving agents just the right context to get the job done, avoiding costly calls, bacteria data systems, and unnecessary reasoning loops.

145
00:23:05,614 --> 00:23:16,580
In our own benchmarks, agents grounded in Knowledge Catalog were nearly four times more accurate while running with up to 33% lower latency and up to 75% fewer tokens.

146
00:23:17,262 --> 00:23:21,260
That's better answers, faster, and at a fraction of the cost.

147
00:23:21,960 --> 00:23:27,340
To supercharge this context layer, we're announcing a new studio experience and knowledge catalog.

148
00:23:28,078 --> 00:23:35,900
You can explore what your agents see, spot context gaps, and review proposed enrichments via an AI inbox.

149
00:23:38,200 --> 00:23:46,220
And stewards stay in complete control with confidence thresholds, automated regression tests, and Git version rollbacks.

150
00:23:46,894 --> 00:23:52,600
Now finally, our agentic data cloud redefines how your technical teams and business users work.

151
00:23:53,326 --> 00:24:02,340
We're re-imagining every practitioner's experience, whether a data scientist, an analyst, or a business user with agentic first experiences.

152
00:24:03,086 --> 00:24:13,444
They transition from taking care of the details to focusing on providing the inputs where their business understanding, creativity, and judgment are most impactful.

153
00:24:14,126 --> 00:24:19,040
First, we're extending Gemini with plugins for data science and data engineering.

154
00:24:19,040 --> 00:24:30,320
You'll just describe the outcome you want, and Gemini generates PySpark, provides notebooks to edit and test the code, and trains the model and fixes issues all on its own.

155
00:24:30,894 --> 00:24:32,360
As you saw, Gemini'd work.

156
00:24:32,590 --> 00:24:38,420
That means business analysts and knowledge workers won't need to write complex code to unlock deep value.

157
00:24:39,086 --> 00:24:43,940
Anyone will be able to run predictive modeling and explore data in natural language.

158
00:24:43,940 --> 00:24:51,760
By bridging technical engineering and everyday business users, we're democratizing data science across your entire enterprise.

159
00:24:52,540 --> 00:24:54,100
Next, operational reporting.

160
00:24:54,700 --> 00:24:57,480
Data insights for everyone, simply by asking.

161
00:24:58,160 --> 00:25:06,640
Across every organization, BI teams are buried under endless backlogs, constantly rebuilding one-off dashboards that quickly go stale.

162
00:25:07,640 --> 00:25:12,180
Meanwhile, business users are waiting weeks just to get answers to basic questions.

163
00:25:12,180 --> 00:25:18,700
We're changing this dynamic with plugins for operational reporting and analytics in Gemini.

164
00:25:20,460 --> 00:25:25,800
By tapping into Knowledge Catalog, Gemini will automatically reuse verified queries.

165
00:25:26,414 --> 00:25:33,240
That means your users get faster trusted answers while slashing token costs and eliminating metric drift.

166
00:25:33,870 --> 00:25:44,660
And rather than generating static snapshots, our new experience for agentic visualization pairs with native BI connectors across Looker, Tableau, and Power BI.

167
00:25:45,678 --> 00:25:52,680
Users will be able to filter, pin, and collaborate around live, interactive dashboards directly in Gemini.

168
00:25:53,422 --> 00:25:59,520
No more competing definitions, no more runaway AI query costs, and no more BI backlog.

169
00:26:00,270 --> 00:26:07,900
Now, for developers who'd rather stay in their own tools, we recently announced the general availability of Data Agent Kit.

170
00:26:07,900 --> 00:26:23,120
It eliminates console hopping and ETL boilerplate by integrating Google Data Cloud tools directly into your developer's preferred IDEs and CLI tools, like VS Code, Cloud Code, and Antigravity.

171
00:26:23,720 --> 00:26:32,820
Armed with native MCP tooling, practitioners define business intent and let agents generate, tune, and test data pipelines.

172
00:26:33,422 --> 00:26:34,680
For example, look at PayPal.

173
00:26:34,680 --> 00:26:39,120
They connected Looker's MCP server directly into AI agents.

174
00:26:40,014 --> 00:26:47,000
BI developers defined metric models once, and agents translated user questions into verified SQL.

175
00:26:47,620 --> 00:26:59,620
They accelerated insights by 50%, collapsed report creation from hours to minutes, and enabled 5,000 employees to query live data with near 100% accuracy.

176
00:27:00,174 --> 00:27:02,820
So the era of passive intelligence is over.

177
00:27:02,820 --> 00:27:05,320
the future belongs to the system of action.

178
00:27:05,840 --> 00:27:11,240
And that's why customers are choosing our agentic data cloud to drive their agentic transformation.

179
